WEBVTT

00:00:04.101 --> 00:00:04.582
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> Hello?

00:00:04.903 --> 00:00:05.511
<v><b>Jake:</b></v> Sarah?

00:00:05.979 --> 00:00:06.778
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> Hi, Jake.

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:09.340
<v><b>Jake:</b></v> Hi. Great to hear your voice!

00:00:09.721 --> 00:00:10.649
How are things?

00:00:11.241 --> 00:00:12.955
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> Oh fine, fine.

00:00:14.016 --> 00:00:15.602
When did you arrive in the UK?

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:16.507
<v><b>Jake:</b></v> Last night.

00:00:17.168 --> 00:00:18.467
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> And how was the journey?

00:00:18.715 --> 00:00:19.474
<v><b>Jake:</b></v> Not great.

00:00:19.841 --> 00:00:21.848
The flight was delayed for three hours.

00:00:22.358 --> 00:00:23.713
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> Oh, poor thing.

00:00:24.566 --> 00:00:26.426
Could you do some work while you were waiting?

00:00:26.928 --> 00:00:29.888
<v><b>Jake:</b></v> No, I couldn’t because there was this American guy called Alex

00:00:29.889 --> 00:00:32.860
who was sitting next to me at the airport, and he kept talking to me.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:34.445
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> Oh dear.

00:00:35.199 --> 00:00:37.067
Never mind, you’re here now.

00:00:37.483 --> 00:00:38.540
<v><b>Jake:</b></v> So, when can we meet?

00:00:39.265 --> 00:00:41.646
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> I’m afraid I’m really busy this week.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.615
The only possible day for me is Tuesday.

00:00:45.034 --> 00:00:47.380
I’m going to London from Wednesday to Friday…

00:00:47.838 --> 00:00:50.227
<v><b>Jake:</b></v> Tuesday. Let me look at my calendar.

00:00:50.603 --> 00:00:53.747
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> Wow, Jake, you put things in your calendar!

00:00:54.464 --> 00:00:56.896
You’re much more organized than when we were going out.

00:00:57.293 --> 00:00:58.947
<v><b>Jake:</b></v> Well, I’m better than I was.

00:00:59.352 --> 00:01:02.379
Although I nearly lost my phone at the airport yesterday!

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:04.902
OK, Tuesday.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:07.598
I’m not free in the evening.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.861
I’m having dinner with Mark Taylor, my old professor.

00:01:11.612 --> 00:01:12.474
Do you remember him?

00:01:13.217 --> 00:01:14.477
It’s at seven thirty.

00:01:14.797 --> 00:01:15.981
I can’t change that.

00:01:16.946 --> 00:01:17.961
How about lunch?

00:01:18.618 --> 00:01:20.119
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> It depends on the time.

00:01:20.828 --> 00:01:24.050
A late lunch would be OK, around one forty-five?

00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:27.925
<v><b>Jake:</b></v> The problem is I’m giving my talk at two.

00:01:28.696 --> 00:01:33.087
And I’m having a breakfast meeting at eight fifteen with some colleagues.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.058
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> Well, morning coffee?

00:01:35.363 --> 00:01:36.734
Or tea in the afternoon, then?

00:01:37.201 --> 00:01:38.146
What are you doing then?

00:01:38.696 --> 00:01:39.499
<v><b>Jake:</b></v> Let’s see…

00:01:40.344 --> 00:01:43.685
I’m going to a talk about climate change at four o clock,

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:47.705
so I think maybe morning coffee is best.

00:01:47.705 --> 00:01:50.452
And then we can try to arrange another time.

00:01:50.697 --> 00:01:54.847
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> OK. There’s a nice new coffee bar in the high street called Espresso.

00:01:55.503 --> 00:01:56.399
Meet there at eleven?

00:01:56.837 --> 00:01:57.594
<v><b>Jake:</b></v> Perfect.

00:01:58.289 --> 00:01:59.683
I’m really looking forward to it!

00:01:59.861 --> 00:02:00.486
<v><b>Sarah:</b></v> Me too.

00:02:01.134 --> 00:02:01.557
Bye.